x86_64-linux  M's and Only's constructors are written inside the class and are inline by nature, so clang emits the C2 variant only and cxx1 emits both of Itanium's forms - the same difference return-copy-balance.nonames and implicit-move.nonames record, see docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "An inline member function is a strong symbol". The names this case exists for - `pass` and `give` selecting the move constructor on their return paths - agree; arm64-darwin agrees on every name and so does x86_64-windows
